&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About League&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;League is one of the fastest-growing technology companies in Canada and the leading healthcare experience platform. Getting healthcare is often the easy part — finishing it is where things fall apart: people book the appointment and skip the follow-up, fill the prescription and stop taking it, get the referral and never make the call. That gap costs health plans and health systems money, and it costs people their health. League closes that gap — identifying what each person needs to do next, clearing what’s in their way, and getting it done, for the 70 million+ people whose care already runs through our platform. Health plans and health systems trust us to do this at scale. Organizations like Manulife, SCAN, Geisinger, and Medibank on the payer side, and Baptist and Shoppers Drug Mart on the provider side.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Manager, Marketing Programs &amp;amp; Events owns two connected things: League&#39;s flagship event, League CONNECT, and the year-round programs that engage the community of leaders who convene around it. Reporting to the Director, Brand Experience &amp;amp; Communications, this role goes beyond running a great event — it&#39;s about designing and stewarding an ongoing membership-style experience for a global community of healthcare leaders, of which CONNECT is the annual centrepiece.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This person co-designs the community&#39;s full calendar: exclusive programming like thought leadership content, regional roundtables, and other member benefits that keep this group engaged with League and each other between CONNECT events. They combine event operations rigor with the relationship-building instincts of someone who has run or worked closely with a membership organization (e.g., YPO or similar) — comfortable with executive-level stakeholders, and able to think in terms of a member journey rather than a single event lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;League&#39;s events and community programs are its most direct signal of market credibility, and the quality of this experience directly reflects our positioning as the world&#39;s leading platform for AI-driven healthcare CX.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll own:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;League CONNECT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end project management of League CONNECT alongside the Director, Brand Experience &amp;amp; Communications — League&#39;s primary brand moment and the community&#39;s flagship annual gathering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the attendee/member experience from registration through post-event, ensuring every touchpoint reflects the elevated, exclusive nature of the community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own digital strategy and demand gen for the event, partnering with internal teams on promotional tactics (email, social, SMS) that drive registration, attendance, and engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply strong digital marketing instincts across the full event lifecycle so the digital experience is as considered and on-brand as the in-person one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the internal Events &amp;amp; Design team and external agency on event operations — budget tracking, timeline management, cross-functional coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage hotel, venue, and event agency relationships — room blocks, F&amp;amp;B, on-site logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own on-site execution alongside the event agency — run-of-show, real-time troubleshooting, vendor coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community Program Design &amp;amp; Ownership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-design and own the annual calendar of programming for League&#39;s community of leaders — thought leadership content, regional roundtables, member-exclusive convenings, and other benefits that extend the community&#39;s engagement beyond CONNECT itself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve what &quot;membership&quot; in this community means — value proposition, benefits tiering, cadence of touchpoints, and criteria for participation — in partnership with the Director, Brand Experience &amp;amp; Communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with community members between events; act as a consistent, recognizable point of contact who understands their priorities and can represent League with executive presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and program regional roundtables and smaller-format gatherings that deepen relationships with members in priority markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curate and manage thought leadership opportunities for members — speaking slots, content contributions, peer introductions — that reinforce their reason to stay engaged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event &amp;amp; Field Marketing Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support production and execution of Ignite, Power Up, and other owned events with the same operational rigor as CONNECT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain consistent standards for vendor management, budget tracking, and on-site execution across all owned events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support trade show and field marketing events where capacity allows — digital promotion, vendor coordination, on-site support, logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Collaborate On&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Director, Brand Experience &amp;amp; Communications on community strategy, CONNECT planning, and program design — a highly collaborative relationship built on clear communication and tight handoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Brand Design on creative execution across owned events and community touchpoints — activations, signage, digital assets, branded collateral.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with sales and growth teams on enablement to drive registration, event education, and tracking against event and pipeline goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with the Content Team on programming-to-logistics handoffs, and on thought leadership content produced for/with community members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the ABX team to align invitation strategy and on-site activation to account priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should definitely apply if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve owned complex, multi-stakeholder events end-to-end — and you&#39;re excited to extend that ownership into building an ongoing community, not just a single moment a year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have program management experience, ideally from a membership-based organization (e.g., YPO or similar) — you know how to design a calendar of benefits and touchpoints that keep senior members engaged year-round.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring executive presence — you&#39;re comfortable being a trusted point of contact for senior healthcare leaders and can represent League credibly in those relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring extensive digital marketing experience alongside large-scale event expertise, and understand how digital and in-person experiences reinforce one another.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re highly organized, deadline-driven, and able to run multiple workstreams — event logistics and community programming — at once without sacrificing quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve managed vendors, agencies, and hotel/venue relationships, and you brief partners clearly and hold them accountable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable managing budgets — tracking spend, flagging variances, keeping programs on track.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love agile, fast-paced environments and move easily across a wide variety of stakeholder groups, from internal teams to C-suite community members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re fluent with AI tools and believe the best outcomes come from humans and technology working together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus points for B2B or enterprise SaaS marketing experience, and experience in healthcare, health tech, or a regulated industry is an asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role may not be for you if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You prefer staying at the strategic altitude and find operational details draining — this role lives in both worlds, and both event execution and member relationship-building require sweating the details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You like long lead times and predictable plans — we move fast, priorities shift, and you&#39;ll need to stay calm and organized when they do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;d rather own a single workstream deeply than juggle many at once — this role spans event operations and year-round community programming simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re looking for a heads-down individual contributor role with minimal cross-functional or external stakeholder interaction — this job is highly collaborative and relationship-driven by design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;CANADA APPLICANTS ONLY:&lt;/strong&gt; The Canada-specific compensation range below for this full-time position is exclusive of bonus, equity and benefits. This range reflects the minimum and maximum target for base salaries for the position across all Canadian locations. The salary range is intentional to account for the performance and career progressions a Leaguer will experience in the role throughout their time at League. Where in the band you may land is determined by job-related skills/experience. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range specific to your skills and experience during the hiring process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Compensation range for Canada applicants only&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$95,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$115,000 CAD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Fluency &amp;amp; Ways of Working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At League, we are an&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;AI-native organization&lt;/strong&gt;. We expect all employees regardless of role or level to thoughtfully leverage AI to improve the quality, speed, and impact of their work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What this means in practice:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use AI tools as part of your daily workflow&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to enhance productivity, problem-solving, and decision-making (e.g., drafting, analysis, coding, research, or process automation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply judgment and accountability&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;when using AI by reviewing outputs for accuracy, bias, and quality before use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuously learn and adapt&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;as new AI tools and capabilities emerge, incorporating them into your ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identify opportunities to improve how work gets done&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;from personal productivity to team-level workflows by leveraging AI effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operate with strong data responsibility and security awareness&lt;/strong&gt;, especially when working with sensitive or regulated information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How this scales by level:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual Contributors:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Use AI to improve personal productivity and quality of output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior ICs / Managers:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Integrate AI into team workflows and improve processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leaders:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Drive AI adoption at the organizational level and shape how work is done across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience using AI tools in a practical, responsible way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and openness to experimenting with new technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance efficiency with quality and sound judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Our employees come from different backgrounds, and we celebrate those differences. We are looking for the best candidates for our open roles, but do not expect applicants to meet every qualification in order to be considered. If you are excited about what you could accomplish at League and believe you can add value to our team, we would love to hear from you.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;. If you are an individual in need of assistance at any time during our recruitment process, please contact us at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruitinginfo@league.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruitinginfo@league.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Application Process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Applying to a role you love can be exhausting, and understanding the next steps can feel vague and uncertain. You have done the hard part of submitting your application; let&#39;s do ours by sharing potential next steps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You should receive a confirmation email after submitting your application.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A recruiter (not a computer) reviews all applications at League.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If we see alignment with League&#39;s needs, a recruiter will reach out to learn more about your goals. The recruiter will also share the team-specific interview process depending on the roles you are exploring.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The final step is an offer, which we hope you will accept!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Prior to joining us, we conduct reference and background checks. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-preserver-spaces=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Additional checks could be required for US Candidates, depending on the role you are exploring.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Here are some additional resources to learn more about League:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://league.com/about/?utm_medium=job+posting&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://league.com/about/?utm_medium=job+posting&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Learn about our platform, leadership team and partners&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://league.com/newsroom/highmark-google-cloud-digital-front-door-health-experience/?utm_medium=job+posting&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://league.com/newsroom/highmark-google-cloud-digital-front-door-health-experience/?utm_medium=job+posting&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Highmark Health, Google Cloud, League: new digital front door to seamless care&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
